---
import '~/assets/styles/tailwind.css';
import CommonMeta from '~/components/common/CommonMeta.astro';
import Metadata from '~/components/common/Metadata.astro';
import Favicons from '~/components/Favicons.astro';
import { getCanonical } from '~/utils/permalinks';
import AsciiRuntime from '~/components/joyan/AsciiRuntime.astro';
import AsciiScene from '~/components/joyan/AsciiScene.astro';
import DitherScene from '~/components/joyan/DitherScene.astro';
const metadata = {
  title: 'ASCII comparison lab',
  description: 'Isolated comparison of baked dither and experimental runtime ASCII.',
  canonical: String(getCanonical('/lab/ascii')),
  robots: { index: false, follow: false },
};
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en" dir="ltr">
  <head>
    <CommonMeta />
    <Favicons />
    <Metadata {...metadata} lang="en" />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#0B0B0C" />
  </head>
  <body class="bg-ink-950 font-sans text-bone-100 antialiased">
  <main id="main" tabindex="-1" class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-4 py-10 sm:px-6">
    <a data-lab-return data-astro-reload href="/" class="font-mono text-sm text-bone-100 underline underline-offset-4 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-accent">← Return to landing</a>
    <header class="my-10">
      <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-plomo-400">Lab / WU13 / experimental only</p>
      <h1 class="mt-4 text-4xl tracking-tight text-bone-50 sm:text-5xl">Baked scenes. Live dots.</h1>
      <p class="mt-5 max-w-prose text-bone-100">Two delivery methods, not a production redesign. The existing J1 loop stays baked; the samples below run the real ascii.rest 0.4.0 library locally: two comparison pieces and a live gallery of the coloured dot scenes.</p>
      <p class="mt-3 max-w-prose text-sm text-plomo-400">Runtime art by bas3line · MIT · <a href="https://github.com/bas3line/ascii" class="underline underline-offset-4">source</a>. Vendor artwork and colors are demo-only, not Joyan brand tokens. No external catalogue or font downloads.</p>
    </header>
    <section class="border-t border-hairline py-8" aria-labelledby="baked-title">
      <h2 id="baked-title" class="text-xl text-bone-50">01 / Baked J1 · native video</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-plomo-400">Controlled composition, brand palette and exact poster. Native autoplay may run without JavaScript; reduced motion reveals the poster. The runtime controls below do not control this video.</p>
      <DitherScene />
    </section>
    <AsciiRuntime piece="donut" title="02 / Live donut · text" description="40 × 22 glyphs in a PRE. Shading comes from characters, using the existing local monospace font." />
    <AsciiRuntime piece="java" title="03 / Live cup · colored canvas" description="42 × 28 cells, palette-indexed red and blue glyphs. Vendor Java mark, experimental only—not a product endorsement or new branding. The package draws its own system-monospace atlas." />
    <section class="border-t border-hairline py-8" aria-labelledby="scenes-title">
      <h2 id="scenes-title" class="text-xl text-bone-50">04 / Live scenes · coloured dots</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 max-w-prose text-sm text-plomo-400">Six of the library's fifteen <span class="font-mono">scenes</span> pieces, mounted live from focused local imports at 12 fps. Each frame is 200 × 100 square cells drawn as dots only (<span class="font-mono">·</span>, <span class="font-mono">•</span>, <span class="font-mono">●</span>) over a fixed palette with ordered Bayer dithering and palette compensation — no ASCII glyph art and no remote asset. They are decorative: the caption beside each canvas names it and says what it shows, and each canvas is hidden from assistive technology.</p>
      <p class="mt-3 max-w-prose text-sm text-plomo-400">The library's other generative family, <span class="font-mono">looks</span>, draws character art in a different ramp and is not dithered by default. Its cost depends on how it is measured: bundling the whole recipes barrel minified (vite/esbuild, gzip level 6) is 324,343 B raw / 98,814 B gzip, and even tree-shaken to a single <span class="font-mono">sea()</span> it is 143,960 B raw / 44,252 B gzip. The package exports no <span class="font-mono">ascii.rest/kit/recipes/looks</span> leaf, and one real <span class="font-mono">sea()</span> example measured +44,134 B gzip on top of this gallery (limit: scene-only + 12,288 B). The cost did not fit, so this trial ships no <span class="font-mono">looks</span> example.</p>
      <div class="mt-6 grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2">
        <AsciiScene scene="night-coast" index="scene 01" />
        <AsciiScene scene="misty-forest" index="scene 02" />
        <AsciiScene scene="desert-night" index="scene 03" />
        <AsciiScene scene="aurora-fjord" index="scene 04" />
        <AsciiScene scene="alpine-dawn" index="scene 05" />
        <AsciiScene scene="ocean-sunset" index="scene 06" />
      </div>
    </section>
    <footer class="border-t border-hairline pt-8 text-sm text-plomo-400">
      <p>12 fps maximum · pauses offscreen and in hidden tabs · static under reduced motion. Play restarts the library timeline. Without JavaScript, descriptions replace runtime art; the native baked video may still animate.</p>
      <p class="mt-3">Scenes draw dots, keep square(1:1) cells, and are replayed at a 12 fps ceiling: the played rate can be lower under load. Their palettes are vendor demo art, not Joyan tokens, and their still frame under reduced motion is the package's own.</p>
      <p class="mt-3">Placement candidates: controlled stories and social assets stay baked; runtime may suit purposeful generative accents beside—not behind—content. Rollout remains pending human testing.</p>
    </footer>
  </main>
  </body>
</html>
